//! Applications and the remote face: the identity model, composition,
//! invocation profiles, resources, the one global interaction contract, the
//! carrier vocabularies, and the ingress paved road.
//!
//! # One contract, projected
//!
//! The global interaction contract is stated ONCE, independent of who plays
//! which role; client, server, session, and carrier surfaces are PROJECTIONS
//! generated by the macros crate (hosts opt in via features), and a
//! projection may not add, drop, reorder, relabel, or weaken any message,
//! refusal, cancellation transition, flow-control state, or completion
//! outcome — a projection that diverges is a defect, not a dialect, and no
//! projection becomes its own only judge. "Serve" is dead as a package and
//! survives only as prose for the remote face; the old type prefix died with
//! it.
//!
//! # The final law (carried verbatim in substance)
//!
//! Paths grant no authority. Packaging grants no authority. Artifact
//! placement grants no authority. Carrier security grants no capability.
//! Routing grants no partition authority. Delivery order is not durable
//! history order. Push is not recovery truth. A disconnect is not
//! nonexecution. A generated client is not a second protocol. An adapter is
//! not semantic architecture.

